WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.950
This is the—

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.290
Okay, okay, okay, okay!

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.330
Good evening
from across the waves!

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.040
Um... Wait...
What’s happening?

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.420
Don’t you
“What’s happening?” me!

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.130
It’s our time to shine!

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.340
Speaker shift change!

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.670
What...? But, I haven’t—

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.510
Move it, move it, move it!

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.760
Everyone,
can you hear my voice?

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.930
‘Kay then,
let’s do the title call!

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.600
C’mere, Kojiro, Nyarth!
Follow my lead!

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.100
Ready, and...

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.730
<i>“Team Rocket’s
Secret Kingdom Radio”!</i>

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.270
...starts now!

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.030
Huh? What?

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.280
The BGM!
Play the BGM, meow!

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.160
Huh? That’s such a pain...

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.250
Sure...

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.790
All right! Tonight’s the maiden voyage of our
late-night live show, “Team Rocket’s Secret Kingdom Radio”!

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.630
I’m the main personality,
Musashi!

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:08.720
And...

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.260
Huh?

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.010
Oh, my turn.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.090
Um, I am...

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:15.350
This is personality number two,
Kojiro!

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.390
And...

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.270
The super personality,
Nyarth, meow!

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:20.060
Hold on a sec!

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.560
If you’re the super personality,
then I’m, uh...

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.730
The super hyper per—
main-per-personality!

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:29.150
What’s a main-per, meow?
I don’t get it, meow...

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.950
Also, what’s with me being
personality number two?

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.910
Because you’re my assistant,
obviously.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:37.490
Surely we’re <i>all</i>
main personalities!

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:39.910
That’s what agreed on
beforehand!

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.830
Did we do that?

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.170
We did!

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.170
Oh, you know
this always happens.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:48.420
Live radio shows
are where demons dwell!

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.340
You never know what’ll happen when you’re on-air,
so you gotta roll with the punches!

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:58.390
That just now made it clear
that the demon here is you, Musashi!

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.560
Hey, you two!

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.310
Argue about that later.
We gotta explain why we’re doing this show, meow!

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:04.310
Oh, that’s right!

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.560
‘Kay! Kojiro, take it away!

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.440
R-Right!

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.190
This “Team Rocket—”

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.820
“Team Rocket’s
Secret Kingdom Radio”...

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:17.700
...is a web radio show aiming to recruit lots of new allies—
a.k.a. Team Rocket agents— around the world!

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.240
She took my line again...

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.450
She’s a demon, meow...

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.080
Anyway! Team Rocket
is a wonderful evil organization!

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.340
And as for all its wonders, the main-super-hyper-main-per-per-per-per-per-per...

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.800
...sonality, me, and her merry men, will deliver them to you with a bang!

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.970
No, we’re gonna blast them
into your listener hearts!

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.970
Wait...

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:40.220
How come Musashi
can read the script so effortlessly?

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:45.190
It’s the enormous passion
she’s putting into this radio show, meow.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.190
And so...

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.980
“Life is short,
a maiden be Musashi!

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.820
“What ever should I do?”

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.320
Hey you,
sitting there thinking that...

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.990
If you’re hesitating,
just leap in with a big “bang”!

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:58.240
Cause we’re Team <i>Rocket!</i>

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.330
And then we’ll...

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.500
<i>Get some new agents!</i>

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.420
Well, now it’s time for
tonight’s opening number!

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.090
“Ichi, Ni, San”!
Take it away!

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:12.340
It’s “One, Two, Three”...

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.230
If I do say so myself...

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.530
That was the best live show ever!

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.280
Sure, <i>you</i> got to
have it <i>all</i> your way...

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:02.280
After a point,
I couldn’t get a line in, meow.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.450
The ending was basically
a one-woman show.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.250
‘Cause you two
couldn’t keep up the beat!

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:08.910
Beat?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.210
A radio show
needs to flow like one!

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:18.420
I mean, the BGM might <i>trick</i> you into thinking
you’ve got a good talk rhythm going...

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.300
...but that’s the lowest of the low
for a radio personality!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.140
A crummy personality!

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:27.970
You’ve gotta summon the waves
from deep in your throat...

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:31.730
...and have those waves
carry your words and feelings to the listeners!

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:35.440
Now, basically, the same idea
can be applied to acting, so...

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:39.610
...for a great actress like me,
it’s as easy as breathing!

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:42.410
A free talk that flows forth
like water, meow...

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:44.030
So, then...

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:46.660
Let’s get to planning
the second episode!

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:47.580
What?!

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.660
We’re doing this radio thing again?!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.540
Of course we are.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.170
It was an order from Sakaki!

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:56.380
Okay, Nyarth!
Read out that order!

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:03.220
“Recruit lots of new Team Rocket agents
around the world!” ...is what it says, meow.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.050
That’s why we need radio!

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.560
Radio goes out
all around the world!

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:10.930
We can spread waves of evil
far and wide,

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.980
dye all of our listeners
in the colors of Team Rocket, and then we’ll...

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.570
<i>Get some new agents!</i>

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:19.820
Right?!

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:23.650
Well, when you put it that way,
radio seems like good idea.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:24.820
Ain’t it?

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:29.080
Hey, Rotom! Tell me how many
sign-up applications we got, meow!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.000
Huh...?

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.210
Lemme see...

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:33.960
Zero.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:34.960
Huh?

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.300
And the number of live listeners
you had was... zero.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:43.470
Also, the number of hits
you received post-airing was also... zero.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.300
Zero?! For <i>all</i> of them?!

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.180
Dahhh...

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.690
Musashi?

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:56.150
What’s wrong, meow?

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.770
Well, isn’t that just perfect!

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.860
In that case, we’ll just have to run
a super popular radio show...

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:05.780
...and make every single person
in the whole world join Team Rocket!

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:23.800
All done.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:27.340
I’m at a good stopping point
with my server maintenance, too.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.600
It’s wound up
getting pretty late.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:32.010
Hmm?

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.270
Huh?

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.350
What’s wrong?

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.810
Oh, it’s nothing,
I just got a notification.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.100
A notification?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.020
For what?

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.690
Listening to the radio
is a hobby of mine.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.730
The radio?

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.320
So I’ve set things up to display
notifications for recommended shows.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.160
The radio, huh?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.490
There was a time when I used to
listen to the radio on occasion myself...

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.660
Whoa...

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:59.330
The reception was bad, so I would put the radio
on my balcony and pull the antenna all the way out!

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.960
You did?

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:04.960
These days, there’s plenty of web radio shows,
so you can listen anytime and anywhere.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:09.050
They don’t take messages
through postcards and faxes anymore, right?

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.890
It’s generally all e-mails.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.720
Now that sounds convenient.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:18.060
Still, to tune the dial at a certain time,
on a certain day, every week...

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.980
That had its own appeal.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:23.190
It was like you had
a special appointment with the DJ.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.570
Yeah, yeah!

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.030
I know what you mean!

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.900
That’s exactly why
I like live shows.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.450
It’s like you as the listener and the show
are connected while you’re tuned in,

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:38.040
almost like there’s an invisible bond
being sent out worldwide through the waves!

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:41.880
Now you’ve made me
want to listen to the radio again, too.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:43.630
Please do!

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:52.340
It’s... done...

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.390
Y-Yeah...

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:58.060
We cobbled it together
somehow, meow...

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:02.520
With this,
tonight’s episode two will be perfect!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.070
<i>“Gather With a ‘Wha-Bam,’ Evildoers!</i>

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.740
<i>“For Here is a Perfect Evil,</i>

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:16.040
<i>“and Over There Blooms a Lovely Evil!</i>

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:20.460
<i>“Yes!
It’s Team Rocket’s Secret Kingdom Radio...</i>

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:23.790
<i>“Alpha Returns... Z!”</i>

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.050
‘Kay, that marks the start of...

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:33.050
“Gather With a ‘Wha-Bam,’ Evildoers! For Here is
a Perfect Evil, and Over There Blooms a Lovely Evil!

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:38.060
“Yes! It’s Team Rocket’s
Secret Kingdom Radio Alpha Returns... Z!”

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:40.810
I’m the super personality,
Musashi!

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.440
I’m the extreme personality,
Kojiro!

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:46.940
And I’m the SS-tier personality,
Nyarth, meow!

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:54.700
This is a live web radio show aiming to recruit new agents
to the evil organization Team Rocket!

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.910
Tonight, for our second show,
we’ve already made some changes!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.290
You can’t miss a moment
of the show, meow!

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.790
So...

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:05.040
<i>“Gather With a ‘Wha-Bam,’ Evildoers!</i>

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.590
<i>“For Here is a Perfect Evil,</i>

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:11.470
<i>“and Over There Blooms a Lovely Evil!</i>

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:16.220
<i>“Yes!
It’s Team Rocket’s Secret Kingdom Radio...</i>

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:19.060
<i>“Alpha Returns... Z!”</i>

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:22.430
<i>...starting now!</i>

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.900
Cut to commercials, meow!

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:31.030
Sign-up applications, zero...

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:39.290
Tonight, I think we failed because the new
“Let’s! Nasty Plot Shiritori” segment didn’t take off...

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.160
And you know
who suggested that segment...

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.160
It was Kojiro.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:47.210
W-Well, whenever <i>we</i> do it,
it always gets us motivated!

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:48.040
So I thought it’d be grea—

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.380
Or, actually...

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.340
This show name is too long!

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:57.180
How about we do that “...or, ‘whats-it,’ for short!”
thing you see everywhere?

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:57.930
Good suggestion.

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:02.180
I think we need some
original greeting for the show, meow.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.100
Wouldn’t it be nice
if we had some nicknames, too?

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:05.900
Ooh, me!

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.150
Go on, Kojiro.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:10.400
Actually, I made us
some memorabilia!

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:12.190
Memorabilia?!

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.400
So what’s that?

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.530
Bonk.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:19.990
Items exclusive to the show, given only to
listeners whose messages we read, meow!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.370
Crown cap-shaped badges!

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:23.950
Wh-What do you think?

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:24.960
Great!

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.170
They’re just so <i>radio!</i>

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:28.130
The listeners are gonna
love these, meow!

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:29.500
R-Really?

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:33.590
Th-Then I thought
maybe this would be good, too...

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:34.630
A Premier Ball!

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.260
Isn’t that a precious
part of your collection?!

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.140
If it’ll make our listeners happy...

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.720
Kojiro!

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.520
You’re a true personality!

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:45.940
All right! Now I’m motivated!

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:49.190
Time for a fault-finding and
plans-for-the-next-episode meeting!

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.230
Let’s do it!

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.980
Yeah!

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:55.240
And so,
through meeting after meeting,

00:11:55.240 --> 00:12:00.160
the live Team Rocket Radio show
underwent many little changes,

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:03.830
and became popular
in radio fan circles.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.250
“Wha-bam Z!”

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:11.420
Everyone,
let’s “wha-bam” tonight!

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:13.460
Wha-bam, hyah!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.300
Tonight is episode 56!

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.380
That’s quite a long-running show...

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:19.390
I’m personality
Princess Number Seven!

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:21.260
This is Mentor Blue-bruise!

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:23.640
And I’m Charm Head-no-suke, meow!

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:31.810
This is a live web radio show where the motto is
“to make friends with everyone across the world”!

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.690
Tonight!

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:34.320
Just like every night!

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.360
We’re starting
tons of new segments!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.150
First up is...

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:40.610
“What’s inside the Pelipper?”,
meow!

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.410
And second...

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:46.200
“Morpeko’s ASMR time!”

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.410
A-S-M-R?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.120
A-S-M-R, what’s—?

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:54.630
Of course, our popular segment, “Solving your
worries with a ‘wha-bam bam’!” is coming up, too!

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:57.630
And with that, let’s go to
our listeners’ messages segment!

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:02.930
Wha-bam name “Daddy’s A Lonely Ball Lately,”
thank you for all of your messages!

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.260
Thank you kindly!

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:08.600
“My daughter is giving all her attention
to Pokémon, and none to her daddy.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.270
“How can I make her
care about me again?”

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.020
Wait, isn’t this a request for advice?

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:16.280
That’s Daddy’s A Lonely Ball Lately
for you, meow.

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:22.280
Submitting his problems to the listeners’
messages segment... That’s a master at work!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.910
Well, um, but...
Isn’t this, uh...?

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.540
Nothing you can do about
someone being interested in Pokémon.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:30.910
Pokémon like Eevee are really cute,
after all, meow!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:31.710
That’s right.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:35.710
If I had an Eevee at my side,
she’d get all my attention!

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.380
Daddy just can’t compare to that!

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.510
You said it.

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:40.970
It’s only natural.

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:43.640
Uh— No, no, no,
that’s not the point.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.010
What should he do to fix it?!

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.430
I’ve got it!

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.930
Why don’t you learn about Pokémon too,
for your daughter?

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.770
I see!

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:55.440
Then why not go all the way
and become a Pokémon Professor?

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:56.480
Good suggestion.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.780
There you have it,
Daddy’s A Lonely Ball Lately...

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:03.570
Set your sights on becoming
a Pokémon Professor, for your daughter!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:07.700
If you do that,
you’re bound to capture your daughter’s attention!

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.700
Try your best!

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:09.500
Wow...

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.540
Now there’s a regular listener!

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.540
This sounds like a fun show!

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:14.120
How many crown cap badges
is that now?

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:18.460
24... No, no, it’s... 25, meow!

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:18.920
No way!

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.630
And you know what that means...

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:25.260
Daddy’s A Lonely Ball Lately
has entered the listener hall of fame!

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.970
Amazing! Congratulations!

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:31.230
If you make it to 30 or so,
we might have to call you our script writer.

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:35.730
“Master at work,” “regular,”
“hall of fame”...

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:41.030
And a success story of going from
listener to script writer...

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:44.280
It’s an avalanche of words
that tug at my heart!

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.360
For the first time in a while...

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.870
...I think I’m gonna get serious!

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:49.700
Next up...

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:53.750
<i>“What’s inside the Pelipper?”</i>

00:14:55.960 --> 00:15:00.590
A segment where we try and guess
what’s hidden inside Pelipper’s beak by touch alone!

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:03.720
And our challenger
is Mentor Blue-bruise!

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:04.840
I’ll do my best!

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:14.180
All you listeners... Listen to Mentor Blue-bruise’s
reactions... and try and guess with him!

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.900
I’ll never get used
to having to do this each time...

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:19.020
Excuse me...

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:21.110
This is...

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:23.650
Flu— Fluffy...?

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.280
It’s... fluffy.

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:26.490
And...?

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:27.870
Yeah, yeah, hold on...

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:28.780
And...

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:30.160
Ah!

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:35.000
Uh... It’s... moist?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.580
What is this?

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:39.080
Ouch!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.590
The answer was a Morpeko!

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:44.300
Did you get it right too,
listeners, meow?

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:48.970
Then, next up is
“Morpeko’s ASMR time”, meow!

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:50.100
Me! Me! Me! Me!

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:51.470
I looked into it!

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:58.150
ASMR are these comfortable
but addictive great-feeling noises, right?

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:00.560
Mm-hmm,
you’ve got the gist of it, meow.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:06.990
So then... Ahh!
Now... Morpeko’s going to eat something...

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.990
Okay? So can you behave?

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:14.040
...so all the listeners at home,
try and guess what it’s eating by the sound!

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:17.460
Got it, got it!

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:19.580
Okay, here goes...

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.080
Here!

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.840
N-N-No! What’re you doing?!
Don’t eat those!

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:30.970
Meow! It ate ours, too, meow...

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:30.220
What <i>sounds</i> like that
when you eat it?!

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:34.140
We were going to
enjoy those after this...

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:39.940
A-Anyway, could you tell
what it was eating, listeners?

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:42.270
No way.
There’s no way to know...

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.110
It was just this crazy “vrrrrr” sound!

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.650
The answer was...

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.740
The answer was...?

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.490
Pudding à la Mode!

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.200
Pudding à la Mode?!

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.700
Pulling ourselves back together...

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:56.120
Next up, a mini-mini segment!

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.830
“Head-no-suke’s
tongue twisters!”

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.580
This tongue twister
was sent to us by...

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:05.130
Wha-bam name
“The Strong, Rugged Rock Man”!

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:08.090
All right!
They read my message!

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:14.050
And my idol, Princess Number Seven,
even said my name...

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:16.600
Your voice is so lovely tonight,
as always...

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.640
Now, I’ll say it
three times in a row, meow!

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:22.310
Traversing tunnels with Tornelos,
tak—

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:24.980
One more try, meow!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:28.240
Traversing tunnels with Tornelos,
taking time to rest with Tornelos!

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:31.740
Traversing tunnels with Tornelos,
taking time to rest with Tornelos!

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:35.240
Traversing tunnels with Tornelos,
taking time to rest with Tornelos!

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.540
<i>Success!</i>

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:39.250
Great job!

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:42.790
I’m... so happy, meow...

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:52.970
Now, we’ll announce the listener whose e-mail
wha-bammed its way into our hearts the most!

00:17:56.390 --> 00:18:00.230
Wha-bam name “Nervousçoise!”

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:05.980
“I know some children
who have these amazing dreams.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.360
“One who dreams of being
a Pokémon Master,

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:12.280
“and one who dreams of catching every Pokémon
and working his way up to Mew.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:16.370
“Princess Number Seven,
Mentor Blue-bruise, Head-no-suke,

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:19.290
“if you wouldn’t mind,
could you give them a message?”

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:19.830
Hear that?

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:21.790
What enormous dreams, meow...

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:22.290
Yeah!

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:22.710
Mm-hmm.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:23.750
Oh, but...

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:25.130
The thing about dreams...

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:28.300
The bigger they are, the more worth it
they are, and the more exciting!

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.170
That’s right, meow!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:32.470
I’m really rooting
for their success, meow!

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:34.180
Me, too! I am, too.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:38.600
If they ever run into trouble,
I hope they’ll rely on Mentor Blue-bruise!

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:42.560
There will be sad times and hard times
ahead, too, I’m sure...

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:48.980
But you can count on us,
and Nervousçoise, to be on your side!

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:52.110
You better treasure those dreams!

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:54.820
Thank you so much
for the message!

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:58.950
Mentor Blue-bruise’s Premier Ball,
and the show novelty crown cap badge,

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:03.120
will be delivered to you by Pelipper
as soon as the show ends!

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:09.340
That was episode 56
of “Wha-bam Z.”

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:10.500
That’s all for tonight!

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.840
Your companions were
Princess Number Seven,

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.260
Mentor Blue-bruise...

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:16.640
...and Charm Head-no-suke, meow!

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:18.260
Through this and that...

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.310
...what a great feeling!

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:25.140
Morning...

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.190
Good morning.

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:29.060
Morning!

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.270
Good morning!

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.190
Morning, Mr. Renji.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.280
You seem more cheerful than usual.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:36.490
Huh? Really?

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:37.700
Did something good happen?

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.030
Yup!

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.530
This little...

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:41.200
Huh?

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.370
Is that...?

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:44.580
Oh, that’s just a badge.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.830
Just your ordinary everyday badge.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.500
Director Sakuragi!

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:52.840
Let’s wha-bam tonight...

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:55.090
Wha-bam, hyah!

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:56.300
Huh?

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:57.720
Don’t tell me, Renji...

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:58.340
Yes!

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:01.140
That’s right...

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:05.350
Right after you suggested I listen to the radio,
I discovered <i>them!</i>

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:07.480
I found them yesterday!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:10.480
Is that...?!

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:12.110
It’s a Premier Ball!

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.400
Where did you get that?!

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:16.150
Oh, you know...

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:19.280
Are you... Nervousçoise?

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.490
I see.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:24.580
Then it’d only be polite
for a master to reveal himself.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.460
You couldn’t be...?!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.420
Daddy’s A Lonely Ball Lately?!

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:33.250
Mm-hmm!

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.130
Through this and that...

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:37.010
...What a great feeling!

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.550
What is all this?

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.470
No idea, but...

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.760
They’re having fun, so whatever!

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:49.140
<i>“Wha-bam Z!”</i>

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.440
Let’s wha-bam tonight...

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:54.270
Wha-bam, hyah!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.360
Hey, hey, listen to this!
The other day...

00:20:56.360 --> 00:21:02.950
Musashi’s group completely forgot their initial goal
of recruiting new Team Rocket agents around the world.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:08.830
Afterwards, Sakaki harshly scolded them,
but they couldn’t forget the fun of hosting a radio show,

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.460
and still hosted “Wha-bam Z”
occasionally.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:13.250
Their super popular radio show
was legendar—

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.000
Hey! What are you doing
butting in on us?!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:16.760
Oh, I...

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:18.550
Were you listening to a thing I said?

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:19.880
No, I, uh...

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.510
I wasn’t listening.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:23.050
That’s no good!

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:26.930
Even if you’re the narrator,
you still have “do”s and “don’t”s, meow!

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.060
I’m very sorry!

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:30.480
Hey, you can apologize later.

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:31.560
Here, take this.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:33.270
Read out our first message.

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.440
Huh? You want me to read it?

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:39.780
Very well, then.
The first message...

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:43.490
This message is from wha-bam name
“The Radio Sommelier”...

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.910
Go!

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:14.370
Oh, he’s really reliable!

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:16.880
He’s like a big brother
to everyone!

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:19.920
A fight!

00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:23.590
Stop it, Hagigishiri!

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:25.840
We have to do something...!

00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:28.550
Did you think of something?

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:31.260
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:33.930
Help Us,
Big Brother Wanpachi!
